.\" The manual page for pdvim's configuration file. pdvim(1) is the program.
.\" View it with: man docs/man/pdvim.5
.TH PDVIM 5 2026-11-21 "pdvim" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
pdvim \- the configuration file of the pdvim document reader
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/pdvim/config.toml
.br
.I ~/.config/pdvim/config.toml
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR pdvim (1)
reads its configuration from
.I pdvim/config.toml
under
.BR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME ,
or under
.I ~/.config
when that is not set, as it starts.
The file is TOML.
pdvim works without it, and anything left out of it keeps its default.
.B :source
reads it again while pdvim runs, and
.BI ":source " file
reads another file written the same way.
.PP
pdvim's own defaults are a file like it,
.IR defaults.toml ,
built into pdvim and read before the configuration.
It lists every setting and every key binding of every mode, and makes a
good start for one's own:
installed, it is in
.IR /usr/share/doc/pdvim/defaults.toml .
.PP
An entry with a mistake is skipped; the first mistake is shown in the
status bar, and every one is printed to standard error.
A file that is not valid TOML is ignored whole.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
.RS
[settings]
recolor = true
trim = true
scroll\-step = 60
theme = "catppuccin\-macchiato"

[keys.normal]
"ctrl+n" = "next\-tab"
"ctrl+p" = "previous\-tab"
"q" = "none"
"shift+q" = "quit"
"ctrl+t" = ":theme catppuccin\-latte"
"g x" = ":set recolor false; zoom\-to 150"

[keys.visual]
"Y" = "yank"
.RE
.fi
.SH SETTINGS
The
.B [settings]
table takes the same names and values as
.BR :set .
Colors are written
.BR #rrggbb .
.TP
.B recolor
Recolor pages for a dark background:
.BR true ,
.BR false ,
or
.BR """auto""" ,
the default, to follow the system's light or dark theme as the desktop's
color-scheme setting says.
With
.B true
or
.BR false ,
it and
.B trim
decide how a document starts the first time it is opened; after that it is
restored as it was left.
.TP
.B trim
Hide the blank margins of pages.
Default
.BR false .
.TP
.B theme
The colors of the bars, the lists, the backdrop behind the pages, and those
pages are recolored in:
.BR pdvim\-dark ,
.BR pdvim\-light ,
.BR catppuccin\-latte ,
.BR catppuccin\-frappe ,
.BR catppuccin\-macchiato ,
.BR catppuccin\-mocha ,
or
.BR auto ,
the default, to use
.B theme\-dark
or
.B theme\-light
as the system's theme is dark or light.
.TP
.BR theme\-dark ", " theme\-light
The themes followed while the system is dark, and light.
Default
.B catppuccin\-mocha
and
.BR catppuccin\-latte .
.TP
.BR recolor\-lightcolor ", " recolor\-darkcolor
The colors white paper and black ink become when recolored, or
.BR """theme""" ,
the default, for the theme's background and text colors.
.TP
.B scroll\-step
How far one
.B j
or
.B k
scrolls, in pixels.
Default 40.
.TP
.B fontsize
The size of type, in points from 4 to 72, that EPUB and FB2 books are laid
out in.
Default 12.
.TP
.B columns
How many pages sit side by side in a document not opened before, from 1
to 4.
Default 1.
.B :set columns
and
.B zc
change only the tab in view, and each document remembers its own.
.TP
.B confirm\-quit
Ask before quitting.
Default
.BR true .
.TP
.B confirm\-tab\-close
Ask before closing a tab while others are open.
Default
.BR true .
.TP
.B autosave
Save markings into the PDF as soon as they are made or taken back, rather
than at
.BR :w .
Default
.BR false .
.TP
.B hintchars
The letters labels are made of, the first used most.
Default
.BR asdfghjkl .
.TP
.B incsearch
Highlight the matches in view while a search is typed.
Default
.BR true .
.TP
.B tabbar
Show the tab bar when more than one tab is open.
Default
.BR true .
.TP
.B statusbar
Show the status bar while reading; off, it shows only while it has
something to say.
Default
.BR true .
.TP
.BR highlight\-color ", " underline\-color ", " strikeout\-color ", " squiggly\-color ", " note\-color
The colors visual mode's
.BR H ,
.BR U ,
.B S
and
.B W
mark text in, and of a note's icon.
Default
.BR #ffff00 ,
.BR #1e88e5 ,
.BR #e53935 ,
.B #fb8c00
and
.BR #fdd835 .
.SH PATHS
Each
.B [[paths]]
table gives the documents whose paths match a pattern settings of their
own: any of
.BR recolor ,
.B trim
and
.BR columns ,
with the pattern under
.BR match .
They set how a matching document looks each time it opens, over how it
was left and the system's theme; where several match, the last wins.
.PP
In a pattern,
.B *
is any characters but
.BR / ,
.B ?
is one, and
.B **
is any characters at all.
A pattern ending in
.B /
is everything under that folder, one without a
.B /
is matched against the file's name alone, and
.B \(ti
at the start is the home folder.
.PP
.nf
.RS
[[paths]]
match = "\(ti/scans/**"
recolor = false
trim = true

[[paths]]
match = "*.cbz"
columns = 2
.RE
.fi
.SH KEYS
Each
.BI [keys. mode ]
table binds keys to that mode's actions, on top of the default keys.
Binding keys to
.B """none"""
removes a default.
Keys put straight in
.B [keys]
are bound in normal mode.
.B :map ,
.B :unmap
and
.B :mapclear
change bindings while pdvim runs, naming the mode first for any but
normal:
.BR ":map visual Y yank" .
.PP
A key is a single character, such as
.BR j ,
.B G
or
.BR ? ,
or a name:
.BR space ,
.BR tab ,
.BR escape ,
.BR enter ,
.BR backspace ,
.BR up ,
.BR down ,
.BR left ,
.BR right ,
.BR pageup ,
.BR pagedown ,
.BR home ,
.BR end ,
or
.B f1
to
.BR f12 .
.B ctrl+
and
.B shift+
in front add modifiers:
.BR ctrl+d ,
.BR shift+tab ,
.BR ctrl+shift+tab .
.B shift+q
is the same as
.BR Q .
The keys of a sequence are separated by spaces, as in
.BR """g g""" .
If one binding starts a longer one, the shorter wins.
A count typed before the keys is passed to the action.
.PP
In normal mode, keys can run a command line instead, written after a
.BR : ;
.B ;
separates several commands, which run in turn and stop at the first
mistake.
.SS Modes
.TP 12
.B normal
Reading: the actions below.
.TP
.B visual
Selecting text, after
.B v
or
.BR V .
.TP
.B hints
Labels on links or lines; letters not bound type a label.
.TP
.B outline
The table of contents.
.TP
.B overview
Every page small, side by side, after
.BR "g o" .
.TP
.B markings
The list of highlights and other markings.
.TP
.B recent
The list of documents read recently; digits not bound open that entry.
.TP
.B help
The list of keys.
.TP
.B prompt
Typing after
.BR : ,
.B /
or
.BR ? ;
keys not bound type themselves.
.TP
.B confirm
Questions such as
.BR "quit pdvim? (y/n)" ;
keys not bound mean no.
.PP
.I defaults.toml
and
.B :help
list the actions of every mode.
.SS Normal mode actions
Every one also runs as a command,
.BI : action\fR,
with a number after it for a count.
.TP
.B scroll\-down
Scroll down.
Default: \fBj\fP, \fBdown\fP.
.TP
.B scroll\-up
Scroll up.
Default: \fBk\fP, \fBup\fP.
.TP
.B scroll\-left
Scroll left.
Default: \fBh\fP, \fBleft\fP.
.TP
.B scroll\-right
Scroll right.
Default: \fBl\fP, \fBright\fP.
.TP
.B scroll\-half\-down
Scroll half a screen down.
Default: \fBctrl+d\fP.
.TP
.B scroll\-half\-up
Scroll half a screen up.
Default: \fBctrl+u\fP.
.TP
.B scroll\-full\-down
Scroll a screen down.
Default: \fBctrl+f\fP, \fBspace\fP.
.TP
.B scroll\-full\-up
Scroll a screen up.
Default: \fBctrl+b\fP, \fBshift+space\fP.
.TP
.B next\-page
Go to the next page.
Default: \fBJ\fP, \fBpagedown\fP.
.TP
.B previous\-page
Go to the previous page.
Default: \fBK\fP, \fBpageup\fP.
.TP
.B first\-page
Go to the first page, or page n.
Default: \fBg g\fP, \fBhome\fP.
.TP
.B last\-page
Go to the last page, or page n.
Default: \fBG\fP, \fBend\fP.
.TP
.B page\-top
Go to the top of the page.
Default: \fBH\fP.
.TP
.B page\-bottom
Go to the bottom of the page.
Default: \fBL\fP.
.TP
.B next\-chapter
Go to the next chapter or section.
Default: \fB] ]\fP.
.TP
.B previous\-chapter
Go to the previous chapter or section.
Default: \fB[ [\fP.
.TP
.B outline
Show the table of contents, to go to a chapter.
Default: \fBtab\fP.
.TP
.B overview
Show every page small, side by side, to go to one.
Default: \fBg o\fP.
.TP
.B zoom\-in
Zoom in.
Default: \fB+\fP, \fBz i\fP, \fBz I\fP.
.TP
.B zoom\-out
Zoom out.
Default: \fB\-\fP, \fBz o\fP, \fBz O\fP.
.TP
.B zoom\-to
Zoom to 100%, or to n%.
Default: \fB=\fP, \fBz z\fP, \fBz Z\fP.
.TP
.B zoom\-reset
Zoom to 100%.
Default: \fBz 0\fP.
.TP
.B fit\-width
Fit the page width to the window.
Default: \fBz w\fP.
.TP
.B fit\-page
Fit the whole page in the window.
Default: \fBz p\fP.
.TP
.B rotate
Rotate.
Default: \fBr\fP.
.TP
.B toggle\-recolor
Turn recoloring on or off.
Default: \fBR\fP.
.TP
.B toggle\-trim
Turn margin trimming on or off.
Default: \fBt\fP.
.TP
.B toggle\-bars
Hide the tab bar and status bar, or show them.
Default: \fBz b\fP.
.TP
.B toggle\-columns
Show two pages side by side, or one.
Default: \fBz c\fP.
.TP
.B toggle\-fullscreen
Fill the screen, or stop.
Default: \fBf11\fP.
.TP
.B search\-forward
Search forwards.
Default: \fB/\fP.
.TP
.B search\-backward
Search backwards.
Default: \fB?\fP.
.TP
.B search\-next
Go to the next match.
Default: \fBn\fP.
.TP
.B search\-previous
Go to the previous match.
Default: \fBN\fP.
.TP
.B command\-prompt
Open the command prompt.
Default: \fB:\fP.
.TP
.B repeat
Run the last command again; with a count, n times.
Default: \fB.\fP.
.TP
.B recent
Show recent documents.
Default: \fBo\fP.
.TP
.B help
Show every action of every mode, and the keys bound to it.
Default: none.
.TP
.B follow\-link
Label the links and markings in view; type a label to follow or pick one.
Default: \fBf\fP.
.TP
.B follow\-link\-tab
Label the links in view; type a label to open its place in a new tab.
Default: \fBF\fP.
.TP
.B yank\-link
Label the links in view; type a label to copy where it goes.
Default: \fB; y\fP.
.TP
.B visual
Select text from a line picked by label.
Default: \fBv\fP.
.TP
.B visual\-line
Select whole lines from a line picked by label.
Default: \fBV\fP.
.TP
.B flash
Type text in view, then its label, to start selecting there.
Default: \fBs\fP.
.TP
.B first\-field
Fill in the first field of a form in view; tab goes to the next.
Default: \fBg i\fP.
.TP
.B last\-field
Fill in the last field of a form in view.
Default: \fBg I\fP.
.TP
.B field\-again
Go back to the field of a form last gone to.
Default: \fBg ;\fP.
.TP
.B next\-marking
Go to the next highlight or other marking.
Default: \fB] h\fP.
.TP
.B previous\-marking
Go to the previous highlight or other marking.
Default: \fB[ h\fP.
.TP
.B delete\-marking
Take away the marking last gone to.
Default: \fBd\fP.
.TP
.B change\-note
Change the note on the marking gone to.
Default: \fBc\fP.
.TP
.B yank\-marking
Copy the text of the marking gone to.
Default: \fBy h\fP.
.TP
.B label\-markings
Label the markings in view; type a label to pick one.
Default: \fBg h\fP.
.TP
.B markings
List the highlights and other markings, to go to one.
Default: \fBshift+tab\fP.
.TP
.B undo
Take back the last marking, or taking one away.
Default: \fBu\fP.
.TP
.B redo
Put back what undo took back.
Default: \fBctrl+r\fP.
.TP
.B next\-tab
Go to the next tab, or tab n.
Default: \fBg t\fP, \fBctrl+tab\fP.
.TP
.B previous\-tab
Go to the previous tab.
Default: \fBg T\fP, \fBctrl+shift+tab\fP.
.TP
.B tabs
List the open tabs; type to narrow, enter to go to one.
Default: \fBb\fP.
.TP
.B reopen\-tab
Open the tab closed last again, where it was.
Default: \fBU\fP.
.TP
.B set\-mark
Mark this place with the letter typed next.
Default: \fBm\fP.
.TP
.B go\-to\-mark
Go to the mark typed next; \(ga or \(aq for before the last jump.
Default: \fB\(ga\fP, \fB\(aq\fP.
.TP
.B jump\-back
Go back to where the last jump left from, or n jumps.
Default: \fBctrl+o\fP.
.TP
.B jump\-forward
Go forward again through the jumps.
Default: \fBctrl+i\fP.
.TP
.B write
Save the highlights and other changes into the file.
Default: \fBctrl+s\fP.
.TP
.B yank\-path
Copy the path of the document\(aqs file.
Default: \fBy y\fP.
.TP
.B yank\-title
Copy the document\(aqs title, or its file\(aqs name.
Default: \fBy t\fP.
.TP
.B yank\-page
Copy the text of the page in view.
Default: \fBy p\fP.
.TP
.B yank\-picture
Label the pictures and figures in view; type a label to copy one as a picture.
Default: \fBy i\fP.
.TP
.B info
Show the document\(aqs title, author, dates and more.
Default: \fBctrl+g\fP.
.TP
.B abort
Cancel a half\-typed command, hide highlights.
Default: \fBescape\fP, \fBctrl+c\fP, \fBctrl+[\fP.
.TP
.B quit
Close the tab, and quit after the last one.
Default: \fBq\fP.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/pdvim/config.toml
The configuration; by default
.IR ~/.config/pdvim/config.toml .
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/pdvim/defaults.toml
pdvim's defaults, as a configuration file, where packages install it.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pdvim (1)
.PP
https://toml.io
